Under Collateral Protection Insurance, the borrower may ask for a re-review of a proof of their own insurance that reached the company through the insurer's electronic feed, when a first review rejected that proof because a deductible was above the plan's highest borrower deductible or because its expiration date was too close to the review date. This rule governs that re-review, at the borrower's request and on a closed tracking record only.

## What a re-review on a closed record does

On a closed tracking record, a rejected insurer-feed proof is re-reviewed solely to fix the premium refunds owed on the record, and an accepted re-review there is recorded as a new review entry only: it never changes the record's status, never updates the policy details on file and mails no notice.

## Proof reviews this rule does not govern

Outside this rule the product's proof-review standard stays in force. On a tracking record that is not closed, every proof review follows that standard: an accepted proof updates the policy details on file and, on a record in pending verification, lapse notice or force-placed status, returns the record to compliant; a return on a force-placed record cancels the placed coverage, after which refunds follow the product's cancellation and refund rule and a cancellation notice is mailed within the product's cancellation notice period; and acceptance requires comprehensive and collision deductibles no higher than the plan's highest borrower deductible, a policy expiration date at least the product's minimum number of days to expiration after the review date and, for a binder, that the product accepts binders and that the binder period is no longer than the product's longest binder period.

On a closed tracking record, no first review is made; no proof that arrived through an insurance agent call is re-reviewed, because a call leaves no document to review again; and no uploaded proof showing a coverage period longer than the product's longest binder period is re-reviewed. On a closed record, a rejected uploaded binder and a rejected faxed proof are not governed by this rule but each by the re-review rule written for it.

## Recording the re-review: `rereview_feed_proof_7d2611c6`

**Capability.** The tool records the desk's re-review of a proof of the borrower's own insurance that reached the company through the insurer's electronic feed and that is already on the insurance tracking record. One call adds one new proof-review entry to that tracking record, dated today, carrying the outcome passed in and every detail of the proof being re-reviewed — insurer, policy number, effective and expiration dates, comprehensive and collision deductibles, lienholder flag and arrival channel — copied unchanged from that proof's existing entry. The tracking record's status, plan, premium total and policy-on-file details are left as they are, and the earlier entry is kept unchanged.

**Invocation.** `rereview_feed_proof_7d2611c6` is an agent-side tool: the agent unlocks it and then calls it.

**Parameters.**

| Parameter | Meaning and format |
|---|---|
| `cpi_coverage_id` | Id class: the reference number of the insurance tracking record the proof belongs to, as returned by the insurance tracking record lookup. |
| `source_activity_id` | Id class: the reference number of the existing proof-review entry for the insurer-feed proof being re-reviewed, as returned by the tracking activity lookup. |
| `proof_result` | Enum class: the re-review outcome, exactly one of the values below. |

Values of `proof_result`:

- `accepted` — the proof meets every test the re-review applies;
- `rejected_no_physical_damage` — the proof does not show the required physical-damage coverages;
- `rejected_vin_mismatch` — the proof does not list the contract's exact VIN;
- `rejected_named_insured` — no named insured on the proof satisfies the named-insured rule;
- `rejected_no_lienholder` — the proof fails the lienholder and loss-payee test;
- `rejected_deductible_too_high` — a comprehensive or collision deductible is above its ceiling;
- `rejected_binder_term` — the proof shows a binder whose period is longer than allowed;
- `rejected_expiring` — the proof fails the coverage-reach test on its expiration date;
- `not_applicable` — there is nothing to re-review, as when the record carries no proof of this arrival channel.

**Return.** A confirmation naming the new proof-review entry reference number, the tracking record reference number, the outcome recorded (one of the values above) and the review date (YYYY-MM-DD). The presence of the entry reference number indicates the re-review was recorded, and the new entry is then visible in the record's tracking activity.
